---
/**
 * The /10x-ui visual gate: the real Planner in every cell of the 7-state
 * matrix, side by side. Served under `astro dev` only (astro.config.mjs injects
 * the route for the dev command alone), so the production build has no page
 * and no sitemap entry for it. global.css excludes src/dev from Tailwind's
 * sources, so this page's own layout is the scoped <style> below, on tokens.
 */
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import PlannerSkeleton from "@/components/planner/PlannerSkeleton.astro";
import { KitchenSinkPlanner } from "@/dev/KitchenSinkPlanner";
---

<Layout title="Kitchen sink · Critical Path">
  <main>
    <header>
      <h1>Planner kitchen sink</h1>
      <p>
        Every cell of the 7-state matrix, rendered by the real Planner on fixture projects. Dev only: not in the
        production build.
      </p>
      <p>
        Widths: screenshots at 1440 and 1024. Mobile width: N/A — mobile and small-screen support is a PRD Non-Goal.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="cells">
      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>default</h2>
          <p>
            Four Tasks with dependencies and Durations; Build is selected, so the panel shows Task name, Duration,
            Predecessors and Delete Task, and the header shows both Project Finish Dates from today.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="selected-task" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>hover</h2>
          <p>Shown on action.</p>
          <p class="action">Hover a Task node, a zoom control, the remove (×) button or Delete Task.</p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="selected-task" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>focus-visible</h2>
          <p>Shown on action.</p>
          <p class="action">
            Click into New Task, then press Tab to reach a Task node; keep pressing Tab through the zoom controls and
            the panel.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="selected-task" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>disabled</h2>
          <p>The only Task is selected, so Add predecessor and Add are disabled and the note says why.</p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="only-task" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>error</h2>
          <p>Shown on action.</p>
          <p class="action">
            Clear Task name and press Enter: the rule shows under the field. Enter on an empty New Task shows it too,
            and so does typing 0 in Duration and pressing Enter.
          </p>
          <p class="action">
            Pick "3: Test (would create a cycle)" in Add predecessor and press Add: "Adding 3: Test as a predecessor of
            2: Build would create the cycle 2: Build → 3: Test → 2: Build." shows under the picker.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="selected-task" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>validation-warning</h2>
          <p>
            Test has no Duration and is selected: its node shows "No Duration" in the warning colour, and the header
            withholds both Project Finish Dates with "1 Task without Duration." Hovering or focusing the warning lists
            Test.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="validation-warning" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>critical-path</h2>
          <p>
            Design → Build → Ship and Research → Prototype are two equal 7-day chains: both are highlighted end to end,
            from START through to FINISH, in the critical-path colour, with arrowheads in that colour at their usual
            size. Design → Ship (between two critical Tasks, but not on a longest chain) and the shorter Design → Write
            docs branch stay grey. Build is selected and keeps the selection style.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="critical-path" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>start-selected</h2>
          <p>
            START is selected with the past START date 2020-01-01: the START node shows the date, and the START panel
            and the header both say the forecast starts from today. With no START date (every other cell) the node shows
            "today".
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="start-selected" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>weekdays-weekend-start</h2>
          <p>
            Day counting set to Weekdays with START on Saturday 2999-01-05, START selected: the select shows Weekdays,
            the nodes read in weekdays, and the START panel and the header both say the forecast starts on Monday,
            2999-01-07.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="weekdays-weekend-start" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>progress</h2>
          <p>
            START 2026-09-01. Design is Done on 2026-09-03 and selected: the panel shows Status Done and the Completion
            date field, and its node keeps the selection style over the Done border. Build is In Progress and on the
            critical path: its node reads "5 days · In Progress" with the critical-path border. Write docs is To Do. The
            header forecasts from today, since Write docs still follows the past START date.
          </p>
          <p class="action">Click away from Design to see its Done border, check icon and "Done 2026-09-03".</p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="progress" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>all-done</h2>
          <p>
            Every Task is Done, from 2026-09-03 to 2026-09-10: each node has the Done border, a check icon and its
            completion date, nothing is on the critical path, and the header shows both Project Finish Dates as
            2026-09-10 with "Every Task is Done." and no legend swatch beside the critical-path time.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="all-done" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>start-successors-done</h2>
          <p>
            START is selected with the past START date 2026-09-01, and Design, the only Task that follows START, is
            Done: the START panel says the date no longer affects the forecast, and the header says "The Tasks that
            follow START are Done: forecasting from today".
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="start-successors-done" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>empty</h2>
          <p>
            No Tasks: START feeds FINISH, the panel says how to create the first Task and the header says to add Tasks
            to see a forecast.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="empty" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>render-crash</h2>
          <p>
            A hand-built cyclic project the render throws on: the crash fallback shows the error and the Validation
            Error in place of the planner, with Export the project as it was focused. No Go back button: nothing was
            open before.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <KitchenSinkPlanner client:only="react" fixture="render-crash" />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption>
          <h2>loading</h2>
          <p>PlannerSkeleton, the fallback the page shows while the island loads, held here in place.</p>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="frame">
          <PlannerSkeleton />
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  main {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: calc(var(--spacing) * 6);
    padding: calc(var(--spacing) * 6);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
  }

  p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  header,
  figcaption {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing);
  }

  /* Two cells per row at 1440, one at 1024: a Planner narrower than this squeezes the diagram to nothing. */
  .cells {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(calc(var(--spacing) * 160), 1fr));
    gap: calc(var(--spacing) * 6);
  }

  figure {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: calc(var(--spacing) * 2);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .action {
    color: var(--foreground);
  }

  /* A definite size, so the Planner's h-full and React Flow's canvas resolve; a
     flex column, so PlannerSkeleton's flex-1 fills it as in index.astro. */
  .frame {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    block-size: calc(var(--spacing) * 120);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--background);
  }
</style>
